{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-295362-r4517909","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Carrot Pudding","sourcePageId":295362,"sourceRevision":"4517909","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T03:13:52Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Carrot%20Pudding&oldid=4517909","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:35:13.004Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for pudding","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using carrot","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"9130bc8e591a62f9ee775f0dd7966c0199116938cffcb922812f99371075ce3c","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Pudding recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}\n\nThis recipe originates from Ida Geller Weiner (1912–2008), of New Haven CT, who made it Thanksgiving and other family gatherings.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n*1.5 [[Cookbook:Pound|lbs]] (1.25 [[Cookbook:Kilogram|kg]] / about 4–5 [[Cookbook:Each|ea]].) [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrots]]\n* 1¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*½ tsp [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n*½ tsp [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Shortening|shortening]], [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]], or [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Egg Yolk|egg yolks]]\n*⅓ cup [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n*1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]] juice\n*½ tsp [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Egg White|egg whites]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n#Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 325 °F (150 °C).\n#Cook carrots until soft, then drain and [[Cookbook:Mashing|mash]] them. Set aside.\n#[[Cookbook:Sifting|Sift]] together flour, salt, baking powder, and baking soda.\n#[[Cookbook:Creaming|Cream]] together shortening and egg yolks.\n#[[Cookbook:Beating|Beat]] in brown sugar, cold water, lemon juice, and vanilla until well-mixed. Stir in mashed carrots, then dry ingredients.\n#[[Cookbook:Whipping|Whip]] the egg whites until stiff, then [[Cookbook:Folding|fold]] into carrot batter.\n#Transfer batter to a well-greased ring mold (with a bottom).\n#Place a large shallow pan with about an [[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] of water in the preheated oven, and place the pudding in the pan.  \n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 1 hour. Unmold onto a serving plate while still somewhat warm.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* If needed, you can substitute baby carrots for the regular carrots.\n* If desired, you can add other chopped vegetable (peas, chopped string beans, etc).\n* If you can't make a water bath, just bake without it.\n\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pudding]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Carrot Pudding","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1.5 lbs (1.25 kg / about 4–5 ea.) carrots","sourceText":"1.5 lbs (1.25 kg / about 4–5 ea.) carrots","amountText":"1.5 lbs (1.25 kg / about 4–5 ea.) carrots","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1¼ cups flour","sourceText":"1¼ cups flour","amountText":"1¼ cups flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 tsp salt","sourceText":"1 tsp salt","amountText":"1 tsp salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ tsp baking powder","sourceText":"½ tsp baking powder","amountText":"½ tsp baking powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"½ tsp baking soda","sourceText":"½ tsp baking soda","amountText":"½ tsp baking soda","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 cup shortening, butter, or margarine","sourceText":"1 cup shortening, butter, or margarine","amountText":"1 cup shortening, butter, or margarine","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"2 egg yolks","sourceText":"2 egg yolks","amountText":"2 egg yolks","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"⅓ cup brown sugar","sourceText":"⅓ cup brown sugar","amountText":"⅓ cup brown sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"1 tbsp water","sourceText":"1 tbsp water","amountText":"1 tbsp water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"1 tbsp lemon juice","sourceText":"1 tbsp lemon juice","amountText":"1 tbsp lemon juice","amount":null,"unit":null,"fo